papers/70-weighted-heisenberg-congruence-nullities/stage4/REVISED_DRAFT.md:227:An additional non-split fixture takes \((\ell,p)=(3,2)\), so the nontrivial cube roots lie in \(\mathbb F_4\) rather than \(\mathbb F_2\). Writing them as \(a\) and \(1+a\), with \(a^2+a+1=0\), exact enumeration of \(1+u+v=0\) gives precisely \((u,v)=(a,1+a),(1+a,a)\). The count two agrees with \[\deg\gcd_{\mathbb F_2[t]}(t^3-1,(1+t)^3+1)=2.\] This independently checks that the ground-field gcd degree counts geometric character solutions even when the roots do not split over the prime field.
